<DnaLibrary Name="OpenAlgo Add-In" RuntimeVersion="v8.0" RollForward="LatestMinor">
  <!--
    ExplicitExports="true" is load bearing.

    With the default of false, Excel-DNA registers every public static method of
    every public class as a worksheet function. That exported the add-in's internal
    helpers into Excel's global namespace under names such as Apply, Read, Error,
    Single, Rows, Cell, Date, Int, Str, Save and Load, and the overloaded ones
    (Apply, Cell, KeyValue) collided with each other, producing
    "Repeated function name: 'Apply' - previous registration will be overwritten"
    in the add-in diagnostics.

    With it set to true only methods carrying [ExcelFunction] or [ExcelCommand]
    are registered, which is exactly the oa_* surface the add-in means to publish.
  -->
  <ExternalLibrary Path="OpenAlgo.dll" ExplicitExports="true" LoadFromBytes="true" Pack="true" IncludePdb="false" />
</DnaLibrary>
